                  %a{:href => "#SupergeometryOfFermionFieldsReferences"} Supergeometry of fermion fields
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            locally modeled on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian spaces
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoints"} superpoints
          %p There are different approaches to the definition and theory of supermanifolds in the literature. The definition
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#AsLocallyRingedSpace"} As locally ringed spaces
          %p is popular. The definition
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#OverSuperpoints"} As manifolds over superpoints
          %p
            has been argued to have advantages, see also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} super ∞-groupoid
          %h2#as_locally_representable_sheaves_on_super_cartesian_spaces As locally representable sheaves on super Cartesian spaces
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supergeometry"} geometry of physics – supergeometry
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+supergeometry#Supermanifolds"} Supermanifolds
          %h2#AsLocallyRingedSpace As locally ringed spaces
          %p
            We discuss a description of supermanifolds that goes back to (
            %a{:href => "#BerezinLeites75"}> Berezin &amp; Leites 1975
            ).
          %h3#definition Definition
          #SupermanifoldLocallyRingedSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong supermanifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p|q
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (|X|, O_X)
              where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |X|
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+countable+space"} second countable space
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi O
                          %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                  of commutative
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+algebras"} super algebras
                  that is locally on small enough open subsets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset |X|
                  isomorphic to one of the form
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                          %msup
                            %mo ∧
                            %mo •
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi q
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^p) \otimes \wedge^\bullet \mathbb{R}^q
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of supermanifolds is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+spaces"} ringed spaces
              (…).
          %p
            Forgetting the graded part by projecting out the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
            (i.e. applying the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic modality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi red
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{red}
          %p
            One just writes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+algebra"} super algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X(X)
            of global sections.
          %p
            With the obvious morphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
            this forms the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SDiff"} SDiff
            of supermanifolds.
          %h3#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/odd+line"} odd line
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
              a smooth finite-rank
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
              of the sections of the dual bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    O_X(U) \coloneqq \Gamma (\wedge^\bullet(E^*))
            %p
              is a supermanifold. This is usually denoted by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi E
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              In particular, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p+q} \to \mathbb{R}^p
              be the trivial rank
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^p
              then one writes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{p|q}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\Pi (\mathbb{R}^{p+q} \to \mathbb{R}^p)
            %p for the corresponding supermanifold.
          %h3#AsLocallyRingedSpacesProperties Properties
          #BatchelorTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Batchelor’s theorem)
            %p
              Every supermanifold is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to one of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi E
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is an ordinary smooth
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Batchelor79"} Batchelor 1979
            reviewed in
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Batchelor84"} Batchelor 1984, §1.13
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rogers07"} Rogers 2007, §8.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Gawędzki77"} Gawędzki 1977 §3 Thm 1 (p 342)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Manin88"} Manin 1988, §2 Thm 2 &amp; Cor 7 (pp 188)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Nevertherless, the category of supermanifolds is far from being
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to that of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
          %p But we have the following useful characterization of morphisms of supermanifolds:
          #MorphismsOfSupermanifoldsByAlgebras.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  There is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SDiff
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi SAlgebras
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        SDiff(X,Y)
                        \\;\simeq\;
                        SAlgebras\big(C^\infty(Y), C^\infty(X)\big),
                %p
                  so the contravariant embedding of supermanifolds into superalgebra is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              %li
                %p
                  Composition with the standard coordinate functions on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p|q}
                  yields an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SDiff
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %munder
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi ev
                              %mo ×
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ×
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi ev
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⏟
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi times
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %munder
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi odd
                              %mo ×
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ×
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi odd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⏟
                          %mrow
                            %mi q
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi times
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        SDiff(X, \mathbb{R}^{p|q})
                        \\simeq
                        \\underbrace{
                        (C^\infty(X)^{ev} \times \cdots
                        \\times C^\infty(X)^{ev})}_{p\; times}
                        \\times
                        \\underbrace{
                        (C^\infty(X)^{odd} \times \cdots
                        \\times C^\infty(X)^{odd})}_{q\; times}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The first statement is a direct extension of the classical fact that
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds+embed+into+formal+duals+of+R-algebras"} smooth manifolds embed into formal duals of R-algebras
          %h2#ModeledOnGrassmannAlgebra As manifolds modeled on Grassman algebras
          %p
            We discuss a description of supermanifolds that goes back to (
            %a{:href => "#DeWitt92"}> DeWitt 92
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#Rogers07"}> Rogers 2007
            ).
          %p (…)
          %h2#OverSuperpoints As manifolds over the base topos on superpoints
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SuperPoint
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperPoint
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoints
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SuperPoint
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SuperPoint
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(SuperPoint) = PSh(SuperPoint)
            its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
          %p
            We discuss a definition of supermanifolds that characterizes them, roughly, as manifolds over this
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Sachse"} Sachse
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} super ∞-groupoid
          %p
            See also
            %a{:href => "http://theoreticalatlas.wordpress.com/2013/07/26/john-huerta-supermanifolds/"} this post
            at Theoretical Atlas.
          %h3#definition_3 Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SuperSet
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SuperPoint
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SuperSet \coloneqq Sh(SuperPoint)
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoints"} superpoints
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ring
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SuperSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R} \in Ring(SuperSet)
            %p
              be the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum"} continuum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
              under the restricted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              of supermanifolds and equipped with its canonical internal algebra structure, hence by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MorphismsOfSupermanifoldsByAlgebras"}
              the presheaf of algebras which sends a Grassmann algebra to its even subalgebra, as discussed at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong superdomain
              is an open subfunctor (…) of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+vector+space"} locally convex
              = succeed "-module." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Sachse"}> Sachse, def. 4.6
            ).
          %p
            We now want to describe supermanifolds as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifolds
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SuperSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperSet
            modeled on superdomains.
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifolds
          #SupermanifoldOverSuperpoint.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em supermanifold
              is a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi SuperPoint
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi SmoothMfd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : SuperPoint^{op} \to SmoothMfd
              equipped with an equivalence class of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#"} supersmooth atlases
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of supermanifolds is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to X'
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chart"} charts
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u : U \to X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u' : U' \to X'
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo ′
                            %mi U
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi u
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi u
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    U \times_{X'} U' &amp;&amp;\stackrel{p'}{\to}&amp;&amp; U'
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p_1}}\downarrow &amp; &amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{u'}}
                    \\\
                    U &amp;\stackrel{u}{\to}&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; X'
                    }
            %p
              can be equipped with the structture of a
              %a{:href => "#"} Banach superdomain
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2
              are supersmooth (…)
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Sachse"}> Sachse, def. 4.13, 4.14
            ).
          %h3#properties_2 Properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The categories of supermanifolds defined as locally ringed spaces, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupermanifoldLocallyRingedSpace"}
              and as manifolds over superpoints, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupermanifoldOverSuperpoint"}
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Sachse"}> Sachse, theorem 5.1
            ). See section 5.2 there for a discussion of the relation to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ModeledOnGrassmannAlgebra"} DeWitt-definition
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-scheme"}> super-scheme
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+super-scheme"} spectral super-scheme
            %li
