                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.07799"}> arXiv:2412.07799
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p (exposition)
          %p
            A more general variant of this in the spirit of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+algebra-ed+topos"} locally algebra-ed toposes
          %ul
            %li
              Alexander Alldridge,
              %em A convenient category of supermanifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.3161"}> arXiv:1109.3161
              )
          %h3#ReferencesOverSuperpoints As manifolds over superpoints
          %p
            The observation that the study of super-structures in mathematics is usefully regarded as taking place over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+points"} super points
            has been made around 1984 in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"}> Albert Schwarz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the definition of superspace
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/links/b12306f831b8c37d32d5ba8511d60c93/tmf5111.pdf"} russian original pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Voronov"}> Alexander Voronov
                ,
                %em Maps of supermanifolds
                , Teoret. Mat. Fiz. (1984) Volume 60, Number 1, Pages 43–48
          %p and in
          %ul
            %li
              V. Molotkov.,
              %em
                Infinite-dimensional
                = succeed "-supermanifolds" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2^k
              , ICTP preprints, IC/84/183, 1984.
          %p A summary/review is in the appendix of
          %ul
            %li#KonechnySchwarz98
              %p
                Anatoly Konechny,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"} Albert Schwarz
              %p
                %em>
                  On
                  = succeed "-dimensional" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi l
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k \oplus l|q)
                , in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julius+Wess"} Julius Wess
                %em Supersymmetry and Quantum Field Theory
                (D. Volkov memorial volume) Lecture Notes in Physics, 509, Springer 1998 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9706003"}> arXiv:hep-th/9706003
                )
              %p
                Anatoly Konechny,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"} Albert Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Theory of
                    = succeed "-dimensional" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi k
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k \oplus l|q)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/PL00001396"} doi:10.1007/PL00001396
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"}> Albert Schwarz
                , I. Shapiro,
                %em Supergeometry and Arithmetic Geometry
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605119"}> arXiv:hep-th/0605119
                )
          %p
            A review with more emphasis on the relevant
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Sachse
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Sachse"}> Christoph Sachse
              ,
              %em A Categorical Formulation of Superalgebra and Supergeometry
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.4067"}> arXiv:0802.4067
              )
          %p
            The site of formal duals not just to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebras"} Grassmann algebras
            but to all super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+points"} infinitesimally thickened points
            is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#KonechnySchwarz"}> Konechny-Schwarz
            ) above and also in
          %ul
            %li
              L. Balduzzi, C. Carmeli, R. Fioresi,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The local functors of points of Supermanifolds
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.exmath.2009.09.005"} doi:10.1016/j.exmath.2009.09.005
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.1872"} arXiv:0908.1872
          %h3#as_manifolds_modelled_on_grassmann_algebras As manifolds modelled on Grassmann algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Katsumi Yagi:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Super manifolds
                %strong 25
                4 (1988) 909-932 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/osaka-journal-of-mathematiacs/volume-25/issue-4/Super-manifolds/ojm/1200781174.full"}> euclid:ojm/1200781174
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#DeWitt92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bryce+DeWitt"}> Bryce DeWitt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supermanifolds
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511564000"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511564000
            %li#Rogers07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alice+Rogers"}> Alice Rogers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supermanifolds: Theory and Applications
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/1878"} doi:10.1142/1878
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (
                  %a{:href => "#Rogers07"} Rogers 2007, Ch. 1
                  that the smooth-manifold-of-(infinite-dimensional)-Grassmann-algebras approach (the “concrete approach”) is identical to the sheaf-of-ringed-spaces approach (the “algebro-geometric” approach) and that this equivalence is shown in Chapter 8. DeWitt seems unsure of this, but is writing more than 20 years earlier, before the ringed-space approach has been fully developed.)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alice+Rogers"}> Alice Rogers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Aspects of the Geometrical Approach to Supermanifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mathematical Aspects of Superspace
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 132
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-009-6446-4_5"} doi:10.1007/978-94-009-6446-4_5
          %h3#other Other
          %p
            Discussion with an eye towards
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+over+supermanifolds"} integration over supermanifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Notes On Supermanifolds and Integration
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1209.2199"}> arXiv:1209.2199
              )
          %p Discussion of global properties:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Louis+Crane"}> Louis Crane
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+M.+Rabin"} Jeffrey M. Rabin
              = succeed "," do
                %em Global properties of supermanifolds
              %strong 100
              1 (1985) 141-160 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01212690"}> doi:10.1007/BF01212690
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1103943340"} euclid:cmp/1103943340
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"}> Yuri Manin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topics in noncommutative geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                , P. Etingof,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"} Daniel Freed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                    , A course for mathematicians
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} web version
            %li#Varadarajan04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Veeravalli+Varadarajan"}> Veeravalli Varadarajan
                ,
                %em The Concept of a Supermanifold
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elementary Theory of Supermanifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supersymmetry+for+mathematicians"}> Supersymmetry for mathematicians
                    \: An introduction
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 11
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/cln/011"} doi:10.1090/cln/011
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+S.+Cattaneo"}> Alberto S. Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Florian+Schaetz"} Florian Schaetz
                %em Introduction to supergeometry
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.3401"}> arxiv/1011.3401
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            There are many books in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            (most well known is by Wess and Barger from 1992), but they emphasise more on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+algebra"} supersymmetries
            rather than on (the superspace and)
            = succeed "." do
              %em supermanifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          %p
            See also
            %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/sachse/handoutbatchelor.pdf"} pdf
          %div
            %h3#SupergeometryOfFermionFieldsReferences Supergeometry of fermion fields
            %p
              Discussion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical mechanics
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+particle"} spinning particle
              or of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
              (possibly but
              %em not necessarily
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} super-symmetric
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %p
              via (possibly
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+manifold"} infinite-dimensional
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+A.+Berezin"}> Felix A. Berezin
                  , M. S. Marinov:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Particle Spin Dynamics as the Grassmann Variant of Classical Mechanics
                  %strong 104
                  2 (1977) 336-362 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0003-4916(77)90335-9"}> doi:10.1016/0003-4916(77)90335-9
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://inis.iaea.org/collection/NCLCollectionStore/_Public/09/348/9348577.pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BerezinMarinov-ParticleSpin.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                %p
                  reprinted in Appendix I of:
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandre+A.+Kirillov"} Alexandre A. Kirillov
                  (ed.):
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Introduction to Superanalysis
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong 9
                  = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-017-1963-6"} doi:10.1007/978-94-017-1963-6
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schmitt"}> Thomas Schmitt
                  \:
                  %em The Cauchy Problem for Classical Field Equations with Ghost and Fermion Fields
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9607133"}> arXiv:hep-th/9607133
                  ]
              %li#Schmitt97
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schmitt"}> Thomas Schmitt
                  \:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supergeometry and Quantum Field Theory, or: What is a Classical Configuration?
                  %strong 9
                  (1997) 993-1052 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X97000348"}> doi:10.1142/S0129055X97000348
                  ,
                  = succeed "]." do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9607132"} arXiv:hep-th/9607132
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schmitt"}> Thomas Schmitt
                  \:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supermanifolds of classical solutions for Lagrangian field models with ghost and fermion fields
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9707104"} hep-th/9707104
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/445574"} inspire:445574
              %li#Freed99
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em What are fermions?
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Five+lectures+on+supersymmetry"} Five lectures on supersymmetry
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/FLS"} ISBN:978-0-8218-1953-1
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/517862"} spire:517862
              %li#GiachettaMangiarottiSardanashvily09
                %p
                  Giovanni Giachetta, Luigi Mangiarotti,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gennadi+Sardanashvily"} Gennadi Sardanashvily
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Advanced classical field theory
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/7189"} doi:10.1142/7189
              %li#Sardanashvily12
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gennadi+Sardanashvily"}> Gennadi Sardanashvily
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Grassmann-graded Lagrangian theory of even and odd variables
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.2508"} arXiv:1206.2508
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gennadi+Sardanashvily"} Gennadi Sardanashvily
                  W. Wachowski:
                  %em SUSY gauge theory on graded manifolds
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.6318"}> arXiv:1406.6318
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1302860"} spire:1302860
              %li
                %p
                  Viola Gattus, Apostolos Pilaftsis,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supergeometric Approach to Quantum Field Theory
                  %strong 463
                  (2024) 156 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.22323/1.463.0156"}> doi:10.22323/1.463.0156
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.13107"} arXiv:2404.13107
              %li
                %p
                  Viola Gattus, Apostolos Pilaftsis:
                  %em Supergeometric Quantum Effective Action
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.13594"}> arXiv:2406.13594
                  ]
            %p
              and more generally via
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+sets"} smooth super sets
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \: §3.1 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Prequantum+Geometry"} Higher Prequantum Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/New+Spaces+for+Mathematics+and+Physics"} New Spaces for Mathematics and Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108854399.008"} doi:10.1017/9781108854399.008
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1601.05956"} arXiv:1601.05956
            %p
              Discussion with focus on
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %ul
              %li#CastellaniDAuriaFre
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/0224"} doi:10.1142/0224
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/CDF91-TOC.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/CastellaniDAuriaFre-ChII2.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                  ,
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"} Daniel Freed
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supersolutions
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                      , A course for mathematicians
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9901094"} arXiv:hep-th/9901094
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/qft-1-2-s"} ISBN:978-0-8218-2014-8
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} web version
              %li#Freed01
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Classical field theory and Supersymmetry
                  %strong 11
                  (2001) [
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/pcmi.pdf"}> pdf
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Freed-ClassicalFieldTheoryAndSuSy.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %p
              and specifically in the context of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} super-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              (regarding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheets"} worldsheets
              as
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Riemann+surfaces"} super Riemann surfaces
            %ul
              %li#DHokerPhong05
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+D%27Hoker"}> Eric D'Hoker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duong+Phong"} Duong Phong
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Complex geometry and supergeometry
                %strong 2005
                (2007) 1-40 [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0512197"}> arXiv:hep-th/0512197
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/ebooks/current-developments-in-mathematics/Current-Developments-in-Mathematics-2005/Chapter/Complex-geometry-and-supergeometry/cdm/1223654523"} euclid.cdm/1223654523
